in a little over a month the PSP's  PlayStation Store will be removed in  North America this follows its removal  in other regions including Europe back  in 2014  you will still be able to purchase  content for your handheld device from  the PlayStation Store website which you  can then access from the download hub on  your PSP but you will not be able to  make purchases directly from the PSP  store you will also still be able to  make in-game purchases after the  shutdown Sony did not provide an  explanation as to why the PSP store is  getting axed this isn't the only thing  that Sony is pulling the plug on the  PlayStation TV has been discontinued in  the US and Europe shipments for the  device stopped at the end of 2015  once again Sony did not provide a reason  for this decision the PlayStation TV  launched in 2014 at $99 MSRP since its  release the micro console has suffered  numerous price cuts you can now buy the  system for $50 on Amazon but it's not  all bad news coming out of Sony today it  sounds like we could be getting another  Uncharted beta this weekend but Sony has  not confirmed this yet for more news  stay tuned to game spot
 

